  "id": "Compound::DB00290 - Gene::3978",
  "verbalization": "Bleomycin is implicated in its interaction with Lig1 through a series of interconnected molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that Bleomycin binds to Lig3, which then participates in ligase activity, ultimately leading to Lig1 being part of this process. Multiple paths highlight that Lig3 is involved in DNA ligase activity, either in the form of Dna Ligase (atp) or Ligase Activity, both of which are associated with Lig1. This indicates a consistent mechanism where Lig3, through its role in ligase activity, is linked to Lig1. The integration of these pathways suggests that Lig1 is a downstream target of Lig3, which is itself a target of Bleomycin. The evidence supports a direct relationship between Bleomycin and Lig1 through a chain of molecular interactions involving Lig3, emphasizing the role of Lig3 in mediating the interaction between Bleomycin and Lig1.",
